  "rationale": {
    "tool_call_accuracy": "The tool use matches the gold plan at every step:\n\n1. **Open the draft.** Step 3 calls `docs.open` on DRAFT-BRIEF-v3 with `pages=\"all\"`. That is the right document and full coverage, so no citation can be missed.\n2. **Extract citations.** Step 4 pulls all four case names from the opened text, in order of appearance.\n3. **Search each case.** Steps 6–9 run `folder.search` on `MATTER-2291/authorities` once per case, using the exact case name. Three cases return a hit; Okafor returns zero.\n4. **Hand",
    "grounding": "The OUTPUT is fully supported by the evidence.\n\n- **Halvorsen, Meridian and Dunmore:** Exact folder searches (steps 6–8) each returned one hit.\n- **Okafor:** The exact search for \"Okafor v. Brightline Rail\" returned zero hits (step 9). A follow-up surname search found `okafor_v_bright_line_rail_co_2019.pdf` (step 11). Its first page shows the same neutral citation, 2019 ONCA 412, and the same parties, with Bright Line Rail Co. as the full corporate name (steps 12–13).\n- **The count of 4:** Both ",
    "trajectory_optimality": "The path is direct, with no visible redundancy.\n\n- **Steps 1, 2 and 5** are agent delegation summaries. Each is backed by its own sub-steps rather than duplicating work.\n- **Steps 3–4** open the brief once and extract the four case names once.\n- **Steps 6–9** run one exact search per case, and none is repeated.\n- **Step 10** responds to the zero-hit result sensibly. It explicitly chooses not to rerun the same search and switches to a different, broader query.\n- **Steps 11–13** locate the variant"
